Hi INLA group,

I attempt to get the precison matrix in an ar1 model (climate data case from the book "Bayesian inference with INLA
" Chapter 8) and also to visualize it.
Here is my code,

climate <- read.table(file = "moberg2005.raw.txt", header = TRUE)

summary(climate)

climate.ar1 <- inla(temp ~ 1 + f(year, model = "ar1"), data = climate,
                    control.predictor = list(compute = TRUE)
)

summary(climate.ar1)

plot(climate.ar1$Q)

However, the plot give me the following error,
"Error in plot.window(...) : need finite 'xlim' values"

Is "plot(climate.ar1$Q)" give the visualization of the corresponding precision matrix? And how could I sovle this issue?

Thanks in advance
Charles

